# A play-by-mail game, the Axis turn: the game starts with the PBM file that pbm-1942-begin wrote
# (tests/data/pbm/1942-axis.pbm), so the title menu offers Continue PBM Game and highlights it.
# The game shows the news of the Allied turn ("New Allied Infantry recruited in Birm'gham"), then
# the Axis side plays October 1942: it recruits twice in its first city and ends its turn. The game
# writes the PBM file for the Allied player, plays the monthly update, shows "PBM File has been
# saved" and ends. The file is the start of pbm-1942-allied (tests/data/pbm/1942-allied.pbm).
#! seed 1942
#! start pbm/1942-axis.pbm pbm
#! files pbm

rule 1 key space

# The title menu: Continue PBM Game. Then the news.
play until 2:W
digest
text c
play until 5
digest
key space

# Recruit: the first city twice, then Esc.
play until 2:M
digest
text r
prompt
digest
key enter
prompt
key enter
prompt
digest
key esc

# END TURN, Yes: the PBM file is written, the month is updated, and the game ends at "press a key".
play until 2:M
digest
text e
play until 2:E
text y
play until 1
digest
repeat space
